# Shot noise. The bunching of every slice is set by the noise alone at the start
# of the run, so this deck does not need to reach exponential gain to be
# sensitive: it differs immediately, and by order unity, if the slices are given
# different random sequences.
#
# The window is 24 slices, which divides evenly by every rank count the suite
# uses. That matters because Genesis extends the window so that each rank holds
# the same number of slices, and a window of a different length would be a
# second, unrelated reason for two runs to disagree.

&setup
rootname=sase
lattice=lattice.lat
beamline=FEL
lambda0=1e-10
gamma0=11357.82
delz=0.1
seed=987654321
shotnoise=1
npart=2048
nbins=4
&end

&lattice
zmatch=9.5
&end

&time
slen=1.92e-8
sample=8
&end

&field
power=0
dgrid=2.000000e-04
ngrid=51
waist_size=30e-6
&end

&beam
current=3000
delgam=1.000000
ex=4.000000e-07
ey=4.000000e-07
&end

&track
zstop=1.0
&end
